  "narrative": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Abortion Pills (2024), published by Amherst College Press, has no recorded citations yet, but it has been downloaded 179 times. Beyond that, it is used in teaching.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Abortion Pills by Carrie Baker was published by Amherst College Press in 2024. Conceptually, the work connects to Pill, Abortion, Medicine, Pregnancy and Biology. The book was recognised: ACLS Open Access Book Prize & Arcadia Open Access Publishing Award finalist (2026) \u2014 History; Political Science.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">OpenAlex records no citations for the book so far.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">In teaching, it is discussed in 4 recorded lectures. It has been downloaded 179 times via OAPEN. It is recorded in 2 library collections. Its subject matter aligns with Gender equality among the Sustainable Development Goals.</p>",
